  <!-- ============ CHAPTER I ============ -->
  <section class="chapter" id="why">
    <div class="chapter-label">Chapter I</div>
    <h2>Why I Started Down This Path</h2>
    <p>This isn't really about retirement. It's about finding ways to get paid on my own terms — and not taking it all so seriously along the way.</p>
    <p>I grew up a latchkey kid in the 80s. Nobody was managing my afternoons. That kind of independence gets into your blood.</p>
    <p>Overall, it wasn't one thing that led to me finding what made me money or let me keep working remotely, on my own terms. It was a series of a lot of different things — most of which show up later in this list.</p>
    <p>I've reinvented myself a few times — foundry worker, mechanical draftsman, a few things since. The last time I needed out, I told myself: if I'm doing this again, I'm only working on stuff I actually want to do. Something that could eventually support a retirement, sure — but in the meantime, why not get paid on my own terms doing things I actually like?</p>
    <p>That's been the last 10–15 years: finding stuff I'm curious about that's also marketable, working with people I like, and letting the rest sort itself out. The goal was never really retirement. It's getting to where — retired or not — I already feel like I am, because I like what I do enough to keep doing it anyway.</p>
    <p style="font-weight:600;">This list is what that actually looked like, one attempt at a time.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ CHAPTER II: THE TRAIL ============ -->
  <section class="chapter" id="trail">
    <div class="chapter-label">Chapter II</div>
    <h2>The Trail — An Independent Income Archive</h2>
    <div class="trail-intro">Field Notes. Still growing — I add to this every time I remember something else I tried.</div>
    <p style="font-size:13.5px; color:var(--gej-ink-soft); font-style:italic;">This is everything I can remember right now. I'm sure I'm missing a few, and I'm definitely going to keep adding more as I think of them — I can't help myself. Consider this list permanently unfinished.</p>

    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Live music (PlanetCorey)</span><span class="fn-tag live">Active, less than before</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">The original side income. 100+ shows total over the years — still playing, just not as much.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Fantasy football blog</span><span class="fn-tag">Retired</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">Where it all started — $300–500/month, mostly AdSense plus a little affiliate income, sporadic and only during NFL season.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Music marketing blog</span><span class="fn-tag">Retired</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">Led me straight into affiliate marketing before I knew that's what I was doing.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Guitar-course DVD affiliate</span><span class="fn-tag">Retired</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">$500+ days selling courses I actually believed in.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Music promotion affiliate</span><span class="fn-tag">Retired</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">A promotion catalog for musicians. Made decent money for years, then it faded.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">AWeber affiliate</span><span class="fn-tag live">Trickle</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">One referral from 2013 still sends me a check every single year.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Landing page builder affiliate</span><span class="fn-tag">Retired</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">Had a couple of good years over $300/month recurring. Dried up since.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Website building</span><span class="fn-tag">Retired</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">Built sites for people back when "website builder" wasn't a button you click.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Marketing consulting</span><span class="fn-tag live">Active, recurring</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">Clients across a lot of different areas over the years — some hourly, some retainer. Still doing this today.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Upwork freelancing</span><span class="fn-tag">Winding down</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">Proved I could land clients from zero — no network, no reputation, no résumé.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Beehiiv newsletter setup (client)</span><span class="fn-tag">One-off</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">The "$500 consulting experiment" — starting a consulting business from scratch, in public — landed by setting up a client's Beehiiv newsletter for $800.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Google Ads consulting</span><span class="fn-tag live">Active</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">What pays the bills today. Covers both ongoing management and one-off account setup work. Took 15 years to become "the main thing."</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Beehiiv affiliate</span><span class="fn-tag live">Active, growing</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">About $6K total so far, $800+ on the best months. Found almost by accident.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Music podcast</span><span class="fn-tag">Retired</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">Paid briefly when Spotify ran a payment program for podcasters — a separate, earlier podcast from the Redefining Retirement podcast I still record today.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Selling music</span><span class="fn-tag">On and off</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">Sold music here and there over the years. Never a living, always something.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Music streaming royalties</span><span class="fn-tag live">Trickle</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">Still collects about $10 every three months. Hasn't stopped in years.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Direct Matches affiliate</span><span class="fn-tag">Retired</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">An early social network, kind of like LinkedIn, with an affiliate/network-marketing model — recurring income for inviting people. A few hundred a month for a while, then it faded.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Facebook ads management</span><span class="fn-tag">Past clients</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">Ran paid ad campaigns for a temp agency and a major furniture brand.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">YouTube channel setup (client)</span><span class="fn-tag">One-off</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">Got paid once to set up somebody else's YouTube channel.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Naming a company (Upwork)</span><span class="fn-tag">One-off</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">Got paid once just to help name a company. Still don't know what they ended up calling it.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">AI one-on-one training</span><span class="fn-tag live">Active</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">Getting paid to walk people through AI tools, one-on-one.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Amazon affiliate</span><span class="fn-tag live">Trickle</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">Been an Amazon affiliate for years now. Doesn't add up to much, but a few dollars trickle in here and there.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">"Proposals That Pop" (Gumroad)</span><span class="fn-tag live">Trickle</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">An Upwork proposal guide I sold on Gumroad — showed people how to write proposals and find work. Still out there, a little dated now, but still brings in a few bucks.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">MusicGoat digital products</span><span class="fn-tag">Retired</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">Some of my very first digital products — the "Sell More Singles Roadmap" and the "30-Minute Fan Finder," sold on my old MusicGoat site. Cheap products, so not a fortune, but real money from something I made.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">Shopify shop (music merch)</span><span class="fn-tag">Live, no current income</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">A shop for my singer/songwriter stuff — sold T-shirts and CDs. Still live today, just not bringing in anything right now because I haven't been promoting it.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-note">
      <div class="fn-head"><span class="fn-name">JobsWinona (local job listing site)</span><span class="fn-tag">Failed</span></div>
      <div class="fn-note">Real demand, real numbers, real failure — the next chapter is the whole story.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ CASSETTE DIVIDER — slot 2 ============ -->
